00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:43,620
You know, it's a green if it appears below it.

239
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:50,140
And, you know, the number itself, if it's a blue color, it'll tell you that it meets your requirements.

240
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:58,780
You know, I use 30 as my ratio. So, anything, you know, I'm looking for numbers above 30.

241
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:05,840
However, I have my settings set at 28, particularly because I want to see numbers like this, 28.52.

242
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,573
It's not a line in the sand where

243
00:13:08,573 --> 00:13:10,443
it has to be above this

244
00:13:10,443 --> 00:13:13,248
number or below this number. My cutoff is around 30.

245
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:18,760
So, you know, if it's 29.12, you know, that's very close to 30.

246
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:20,880
I want to look at the individual numbers themselves.

247
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,880
It's more of a guideline.

248
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,800
But, you know, definitely

249
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,300
if it's above 30. But if

250
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,100
it's a number between, you know,

251
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,300
28 and 30, I'm also interested

252
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:31,300
in taking a look at it, you know, further review.

253
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:37,500
Okay, the next one is large prints.

254
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:41,325
Bullish large prints appearing at the bottom edges of a

255
00:13:41,325 --> 00:13:44,610
move down are indicative of strong passive buyers appearing in

256
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:51,180
a down move. Aggressive sellers can't move the market through the price level where the strong passive buyers are sitting.

257
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:55,020
So, you guys see that as a ratio. Again, it's going to be blue.

258
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:58,515
Unlike a small print, it's a different type

259
00:13:58,515 --> 00:14:01,258
of number. It's going to be a

260
00:14:01,258 --> 00:14:04,001
number closer to zero, usually a number

261
00:14:04,001 --> 00:14:10,663
between 0.69 or 0.7 and 0, which will indicate that there's heavy volume at the very bottom of the bar.

262
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,420
Now, it's not something you see very often.

263
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,542
You know, over

264
00:14:16,542 --> 00:14:18,289
the course of a day, you may get only

265
00:14:18,289 --> 00:14:21,978
a couple of bars like that. But when it happens at the end of a move, it's very important.

266
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:26,640
It's telling you there's a strong passive participant there who's willing to support the market.

267
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:29,870
Now, large prints appearing at the top of

268
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:35,119
an up move are indicative of strong passive sellers, like you see here.

269
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:42,200
You know, you have a ratio 0.53. It's indicating strong passive buyers up here at the very top of the bar.

270
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,124
These people have a lot of supply to

271
00:14:47,124 --> 00:14:49,268
sell. So, aggressive buyers are not able to

272
00:14:49,268 --> 00:14:51,144
move the market through the price level

273
00:14:51,144 --> 00:14:54,360
where these sellers are sitting. So, buyers can't get it any higher.

274
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,580
Someone has a lot to sell, and they're willing to hold down the market there.

275
00:15:00,470 --> 00:15:01,685
Stack selling imbalances around

276
00:15:01,685 --> 00:15:04,115
highs. Stack selling imbalances that occur after a

277
00:15:04,115 --> 00:15:08,368
recent high is usually a clear indication of a shift in supply and demand.

278
00:15:08,530 --> 00:15:12,950
Buyers have moved the market higher, but aggressive sellers have come in to overwhelm the buyers.

279
00:15:13,690 --> 00:15:16,410
Like I said, I like to take shorts

280
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:18,450
near highs and longs near lows.

281
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:23,550
You don't always get the chance, but I like to have reasons to do it.

282
00:15:23,550 --> 00:15:26,318
And if I'm seeing a stack selling imbalance near a

283
00:15:26,318 --> 00:15:29,086
high, I'm more inclined to take it than a stack

284
00:15:29,086 --> 00:15:34,069
selling imbalance near the low. Because that's where you're going to see a shift in supply and demand.

285
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:38,470
You're going to see shifts around the highs or around the lows.

286
00:15:38,690 --> 00:15:39,472
You know, when

287
00:15:39,472 --> 00:15:41,297
demand near a high, it's demand, demand,

288
00:15:41,297 --> 00:15:44,948
demand. You get it to the high, then all of a sudden there's supply.

289
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:49,710
And the market sells off, and it becomes, you know, supply side taking over.

290
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,530
You know, then

291
00:15:53,530 --> 00:15:55,420
the opposite would be stacking buying imbalances

292
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,580
around the lows. A stacking imbalance, buying imbalance

293
00:15:57,580 --> 00:16:02,440
that occurs after a recent low is usually a clear indication of a shift in supply and demand.

294
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:06,580
It's gone from a supply market to a demand market.

295
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:10,860
Sellers have moved the market lower, but aggressive buyers have come in to overwhelm the sellers.

296
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:11,403
You know,

297
00:16:11,403 --> 00:16:12,218
again, you know,

298
00:16:12,218 --> 00:16:13,577
we're working our way down

299
00:16:13,577 --> 00:16:14,936
towards this low area, and

300
00:16:14,936 --> 00:16:16,295
all of a sudden the

301
00:16:16,295 --> 00:16:17,654
buyers, you know, sit up

302
00:16:17,654 --> 00:16:25,537
and say, Hey, this is a good deal. I want to buy some more. And everyone's aggressive and buying it, and the market moves higher. It should move higher.

303
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:33,740
Divergence. Now, there's two types of divergence. There's bullish divergence. There's bearish divergence.

304
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,811
Bullish divergence occurs when a new or

305
00:16:35,811 --> 00:16:37,190
equal low is made in

306
00:16:37,190 --> 00:16:41,879
the market. The delta is positive, and the bar close higher than the level where it opened.

307
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:46,663
Now, in a market that's trending, you're

308
00:16:46,663 --> 00:16:49,846
going to get divergences, either buying divergences

309
00:16:49,846 --> 00:16:52,574
or selling divergences. And I tend

310
00:16:52,574 --> 00:17:00,759
to like to not just take every divergence by itself. I like to get ratios involved in there.

311
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,030
Like here, you

312
00:17:02,030 --> 00:17:03,247
don't necessarily have a ratio.

313
00:17:03,247 --> 00:17:04,951
You have an imbalance. You know, I

314
00:17:04,951 --> 00:17:06,655
like that I get a little something

315
00:17:06,655 --> 00:17:11,038
extra besides just divergence because there are days when the market just seems like it's a one-way street.

316
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:11,879
And, you know,

317
00:17:11,879 --> 00:17:13,838
if you're trying to sell every divergence

318
00:17:13,838 --> 00:17:18,317
and the market keeps on rallying, you're going to end up in the poorhouse pretty quick.

319
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:21,574
But, you know, just

320
00:17:21,574 --> 00:17:23,846
for explanation's sake, a divergence occurs

321
00:17:23,846 --> 00:17:25,739
when you have a positive

322
00:17:25,739 --> 00:17:31,419
delta at a new low. You should have a negative delta at a new low.

323
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,068
Now, a bearish divergence, again,

324
00:17:33,068 --> 00:17:34,716
it's the opposite, occurs when

325
00:17:34,716 --> 00:17:36,364
a new or equal high

326
00:17:36,364 --> 00:17:41,968
is made in the market. The delta is negative. The bar close lower than where it opened.

327
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:48,390
So, again, here's your new high. You have a delta. That's this down triangle. And you got a negative delta.

328
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:54,168
Now, one of the things that makes my

329
00:17:54,168 --> 00:17:56,529
software a little bit different than most

330
00:17:56,529 --> 00:17:58,890
of the software on the market, it

331
00:17:58,890 --> 00:18:00,914
refers to divergences, most divergence, most

332
00:18:00,914 --> 00:18:03,275
order flow software will just say you

333
00:18:03,275 --> 00:18:11,708
have a divergence when you have a new or equal high and a negative delta or a new or equal low and a positive delta.

334
00:18:11,890 --> 00:18:14,336
I'd like to take it a step further.

335
00:18:14,336 --> 00:18:19,229
I want to see price action in the individual bar confirm the direction of the market.

336
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:27,830
So, you know, if I'm taking a bearish divergence at a high, I want to see the bar close negative.

337
00:18:28,030 --> 00:18:29,270
I don't want to see it close positive.

338
00:18:29,430 --> 00:18:31,370
I don't want the bar to be trading up near the high.

339
00:18:31,450 --> 00:18:33,390
I'd want it to be closing negative.

340
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:39,590
I mean, that's just, for me, just a little extra visual step as far as confirmation.

341
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:51,720
Okay, so bullish extreme imbalances is when you have a bullish extreme imbalance.

342
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:55,160
It occurs when there's a selling imbalance at the bottom of a bar that closed higher than it opened.

343
00:18:55,540 --> 00:19:00,680
On the order flows trader software, it's going to be highlighted with an arrow.

344
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,700
In this case, you know,

345
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:04,200
you'll see the normal selling

346
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,400
imbalance and the bar

347
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,800
closed higher. You know, you'll draw the arrow.

348
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,130
To me, that's a

349
00:19:09,130 --> 00:19:10,585
sign that, you know, sellers are

350
00:19:10,585 --> 00:19:12,040
really aggressive at the bottom of

351
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,495
the bar, you know, and trying

352
00:19:13,495 --> 00:19:17,618
to push the market lower, but it couldn't go any lower and the market popped back up.

353
00:19:17,620 --> 00:19:20,075
The opposite would be a bearish extreme

354
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:22,880
imbalance where, at the top, there is a

355
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:27,088
buying imbalance of a bar that closed lower than where it opens.

356
00:19:27,210 --> 00:19:28,770
Again, here, it's going to draw the arrow.

357
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:37,610
My order flows software is the only software that I'm aware of that draws those arrows and highlights to you.

358
00:19:37,670 --> 00:19:38,588
People say, oh, that's

359
00:19:38,588 --> 00:19:39,736
trap traders. You know, it

360
00:19:39,736 --> 00:19:41,113
is and it isn't. It's people

361
00:19:41,113 --> 00:19:43,868
that are long and wrong and can't move the market any further.

362
00:19:43,870 --> 00:19:51,230
Okay, so, you know, bearish extreme imbalance, when it occurs, I mean, look to get short.

363
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:54,090
It's a quick trade.

364
00:19:54,230 --> 00:19:54,810
It's a quick reversal.

365
00:19:55,010 --> 00:19:57,519
I don't expect these extreme imbalances, the

366
00:19:57,519 --> 00:20:00,028
bullish or bearish ones, to be really

367
00:20:00,028 --> 00:20:04,688
the end of a long-term trend or the start of a new trend.

368
00:20:04,930 --> 00:20:12,430
For me, the bearish extreme imbalances are more of a short-term indicator than a longer-term indicator.

369
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:15,584
I said it'll occur at the end of

370
00:20:15,584 --> 00:20:18,738
a trend pretty quick, and you'll get a

371
00:20:18,738 --> 00:20:21,892
slight move, but it's not a pure reversal

372
00:20:21,892 --> 00:20:27,807
indicator that will indicate the end of a trend and start of a new trend.

373
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:29,469
You know, oftentimes,

374
00:20:29,469 --> 00:20:31,800
a reversal indicator will signal the end

375
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,798
of a trend, but it doesn't

376
00:20:33,798 --> 00:20:37,128
necessarily mean that it's the beginning of a new trend.

377
00:20:40,810 --> 00:20:44,710
Divergence trading sounds great and straightforward, but there are caveats with it.

378
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:46,572
You know, like

379
00:20:46,572 --> 00:20:48,725
I was talking about earlier, in a

380
00:20:48,725 --> 00:20:50,263
trending market, there's going to

381
00:20:50,263 --> 00:20:52,108
be a lot of divergences appearing.

382
00:20:53,270 --> 00:20:55,199
I like to get a little bit

383
00:20:55,199 --> 00:20:57,128
extra out of the divergence rather than

384
00:20:57,128 --> 00:20:59,333
just having a divergence because, you know, say

385
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:03,468
a market is rallying, right, but people are going to take profits at some point.

386
00:21:03,910 --> 00:21:07,910
You will get a negative delta, and, you know, that'll kick off the divergence.

387
00:21:07,910 --> 00:21:10,148
I want to see price being

388
00:21:10,148 --> 00:21:12,386
rejected, so I want to see

389
00:21:12,386 --> 00:21:14,624
a ratio, you know, just occurring

390
00:21:14,624 --> 00:21:18,728
when, either as soon as the divergence occurs or shortly thereafter.

391
00:21:18,730 --> 00:21:24,890
So, in a rapidly trending market, there will be failed divergences, and that's just a fact of life.

392
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:29,070
Divergences with single prints, small prints, large prints are more selective and more powerful.

393
00:21:29,070 --> 00:21:35,890
When you're making new highs, you should see aggressive buying in the form of stacked buying imbalances.

394
00:21:36,010 --> 00:21:40,530
When you're making new lows, you should be seeing aggressive selling in the form of selling imbalances.

395
00:21:40,530 --> 00:21:49,690
Usually, a shift in supply and demand is occurring and can be seen in stacked imbalances.

396
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,800
So, when you're seeing

397
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:54,338
a stacked imbalance, I mean, by definition,

398
00:21:54,338 --> 00:21:57,238
what is a stacked imbalance? A stacked imbalance

399
00:21:57,238 --> 00:22:01,588
is usually three or more imbalances occurring on top of each other.

400
00:22:02,710 --> 00:22:03,819
Now, you can have,

401
00:22:03,819 --> 00:22:05,482
in a bar, you can have

402
00:22:05,482 --> 00:22:07,423
three imbalances. Maybe they're not stacked on

403
00:22:07,423 --> 00:22:12,968
each other. You know, it could be, you know, two, and then a normal price level, and then another one.

404
00:22:13,510 --> 00:22:14,158
But usually,

405
00:22:14,158 --> 00:22:16,751
I mean, visually, seeing a stacked imbalance is

406
00:22:16,751 --> 00:22:19,344
slightly more important because usually it's somebody that's

407
00:22:19,344 --> 00:22:21,289
buying it up through a level.

408
00:22:22,070 --> 00:22:23,906
And when I say a shift

409
00:22:23,906 --> 00:22:26,354
in supply and demand is occurring, you know,

410
00:22:26,354 --> 00:22:31,250
when you see an imbalance occurring, a selling imbalance occurring at a high, think about it.

411
00:22:31,250 --> 00:22:31,690
What's happened?

412
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:35,730
The markets rallied up, made a high as people were buying.

413
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:36,850
The demand was there,

414
00:22:36,850 --> 00:22:39,090
but then you plateau at a high, and

415
00:22:39,090 --> 00:22:41,330
all of a sudden, you see selling come

416
00:22:41,330 --> 00:22:44,410
in, and it's very aggressive in the form of selling imbalances.

417
00:22:44,950 --> 00:22:46,550
Well, the sellers have taken over now.

418
00:22:46,710 --> 00:22:49,430
They're laying off their excess supply in the market.

419
00:22:51,510 --> 00:22:54,450
And the same is true for at a low.

420
00:22:54,450 --> 00:22:56,415
If you see a buying imbalance,

421
00:22:56,415 --> 00:22:59,035
that buying imbalance come in off a low,

422
00:22:59,035 --> 00:23:02,310
you're seeing demand pick up and demand being very aggressive.

423
00:23:03,230 --> 00:23:03,670
So, you

424
00:23:03,670 --> 00:23:05,430
know, I said I prefer to take them

425
00:23:05,430 --> 00:23:06,970
in context of the market. You know,

426
00:23:06,970 --> 00:23:10,270
I'd rather take a buying imbalance near a low, a selling imbalance near the high.

427
00:23:12,830 --> 00:23:13,333
Okay, so

428
00:23:13,333 --> 00:23:15,096
reversal setups. You know, I'll just go

429
00:23:15,096 --> 00:23:16,859
through a bunch of examples here just

